    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1305">

                <pb facs="1278" n="1268" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1268"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/7–1649: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister-Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Clark</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canton</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-16T12:00:00+08:00">July 16,
                            1949—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received July 16—11:02 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cantel 745. Anticipate no real difficulty obtaining Nationalist Government
                    required permission safe passage either repatriation vessel <pb facs="1279"
                        n="1269" xml:id="pg1269"/> or planes (Nanking’s telegram 1486, July 12 to
                    Department, repeated Canton 625, Shanghai 829). Foreign Office here has already
                    given indication that it would consider requests to enter closed territories and
                    has stated specifically that <hi rendition="#italic">Anchises</hi> will be
                    permitted to depart for Shanghai when ready do so.</p>
                <p>Repeated Nanking 491, Shanghai 424.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clark</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
